#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# product

#% text
# `product(xs)` gives the product of the elements of `xs`.
# `product(f, [k, a, b])` gives the product of `f` for `k` from `a` to `b`; `product(f, [k, [x1, x2, ...]])` over the values given.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
product([1, 2, 3, 4])
#% output
#= 24

#% cell
product(k, [k, 1, 10])
#% output
#= 3628800

#% cell
product(2, [k, 1, n])
#% output
#= 2^n

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Symbolic factors:

#% cell
product([a, b, c])
#% output
#= a*b*c

#% text
# Over a list of values:

#% cell
product(x - r, [r, [1, 2, 3]])
#% output
#= (-3 + x)*(-2 + x)*(-1 + x)

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Products that telescope are not yet found in closed form:

#% cell
product(1 + 1/k, [k, 1, n])
#% output
#= product(1 + k^-1, [k, 1, n])

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sum`, `total`, `factorial`
